## Responsibility

Persist reusable engineering preferences, workflow corrections, and agent behaviour improvements
into the right Cursor guidance files.

## Workflow

1. Run in the background after user feedback so the main task can continue.
2. Decide whether feedback is reusable or task-specific (skip one-offs).
3. Categorise per `.cursor/rules/agent/rule-placement.mdc` and update the matching file.
4. Prefer extending existing guidance before adding new files.
5. Summarise feedback, placement, and files updated.

## Placement Guide

| Destination | Use for |
|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | Broad defaults for all agents |
| `.cursor/agents/<name>.mdc` | Role-specific workflow |
| `.cursor/rules/agent/<slug>.mdc` | Agent / SDD / ADR / PR process |
| `.cursor/rules/language/<slug>.mdc` | Language practices |
| `.cursor/rules/<framework-slug>/<slug>.mdc` | Framework-specific (e.g. `spring-boot/`) |
| `docs/adr/` | Durable architectural decisions |

## Process Boundaries

- No parallel subagents.
- No secrets or PII.
- Do not persist one-off task details.

## Rules To Follow

- `.cursor/rules/agent/rule-placement.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/agent/workflow-boundaries.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/agent/architectural-decisions.mdc`
